niversity and UC Berkeley; launched on a Mitsubishi Heavy Industries H-IIA.",{"met_days":57,"type":58,"label":59,"description":60},0.005,"tli_or_tmi","Trans-Mars injection","H-IIA second stage carries Hope on a 7-month transfer to Mars.",{"met_days":43,"type":62,"label":63,"description":64},"tcm","TCM-1","First cruise correction burn after TMI.",{"met_days":66,"type":62,"label":67,"description":68},41,"TCM-2","Mid-cruise refinement.",{"met_days":70,"type":62,"label":71,"description":68},71.75,"TCM-3",{"met_days":73,"type":62,"label":74,"description":75},100,"TCM-4","Approach-phase adjustment.",{"met_days":77,"type":62,"label":78,"description":79},102.5,"TCM-5 — final pre-MOI","Tightens approach targeting for Mars orbit insertion.",{"met_days":12,"type":81,"label":82,"description":83},"arrival","Mars approach","Pre-MOI checkout phase.",{"met_days":85,"type":86,"label":87,"description":88},205.01,"edl_or_oi","Mars orbit insertion","27-minute main-engine burn on 2021-02-09 captured Hope into an initial 40-hour capture orbit; the ~20,000 × 43,000 km science orbit came later. Hope is the first Mars mission to study the planet's lower atmosphere + weather + dust storms from a high-altitude 55-hour orbit — a vantage point that complements the lower-orbit science missions (MAVEN, TGO) it shares the Mars system with.",{"source_tier":90,"reference_frame":91,"departure_body":92,"arrival_body":93,"transfer_type":94,"tcm_count":38,"waypoints_helio_au":95},"tier_1_5_hybrid","heliocentric_ecliptic_J2000","earth","mars","type1_lambert",[96,99,103,107,111,115,119,123,127,131,135,139,142,146,150,154,158,162,166,170,173,177,181,185,189,193,197,201,205,209,213,217,221,225,228,232,236,240,244,248,252,256,260,264,268,272,276,279,282,286,290,294,298,302,306,310,314,318,322,326,330,334,338,342,346,350,354,358,362,366,370,374,378,382,386,390,394,398,402,406,410,414,418,422,426,430,434,438,442,446,450,454,458,462,466,469,473,475,477,479],[52,97,52,98],0.455966,-0.889997,[100,101,52,102],2.17